<http://digistrucmed.org/semantic-unit/lu_66b005a6484e5a6e96e40015102d69efc8bc0d0cc9a2a807f86d748d49b3068d_n0058> <http://digistrucmed.org/titleOrContext> "ial defined target dose.<sup>1-9,11-14</sup> Repeated attempts at uptitration can result in optimization, even if initial attempts may fail. In patients with HFrEF, beta blockers provide dose-dependent improvements in LVEF, reduction in HF hospitalizations, and reduction in all-cause mortality.<sup>17</sup> Trials of lower versus higher dose of ACEi and ARB have shown lower risk of cardiovascular death or HF hospitalization with higher doses, with similar safety and tolerability.<sup>17,18</sup>" .
